From d409b7e46d775e695cd91407859b7cb6b9f22b74 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 09:47:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban: CI-run sweep binds the dispatching home;
 per-home no-credential warning; "gh not installed" wording

PR #2039 review follow-ups (review 5888753558):

1. submit_sweep ran _sweep_db on a pool thread, which does not inherit the
   dispatcher thread's context-local home, so dispatcher_gh_argv() read the
   launch home's kanban.pr_acceptance.gh_command_prefix for every board.
   submit_sweep now resolves the home on the dispatcher thread and _sweep_db
   binds it (bind_profile_scope, no secret hydration).
2. _WARNED_AT was one process-global timestamp, so one home's hourly
   no-credential WARNING hid another's. It is now keyed by (home, board db).
3. A missing gh binary raised NoCredential, whose WARNING told the operator to
   set gh_command_prefix or log gh in. kanban_gh_argv now raises
   GhNotInstalled (a GhArgvUnavailable subclass), surfaced as Progress.gh_missing
   with a "gh not installed: ... Install the GitHub CLI" WARNING.
4. Docs: dispatcher-side GitHub reads (PR state, CI-run progress) use the
   dispatcher home's gh_command_prefix, not the assignee's.

Tests (tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_ci_progress.py), each RED before the fix:
test_sweep_on_a_pool_thread_uses_the_dispatching_homes_prefix,
test_no_credential_warning_is_per_home,
test_missing_gh_warns_gh_not_installed_not_a_credential_fix.
